## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Likely cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Download stops or a file is reported BROKEN | Network interruption or terminal closed | Delete the broken file, rerun `download_fastq.sh` (inside `screen` or with `nohup`) |
| `Cannot find .../raw_data` | `raw_data/` missing, or script not inside `training/scripts/` | Run `mkdir -p raw_data` from `training/`; keep the scripts in `scripts/` |
| STAR: cannot open the FASTA or GTF | Reference missing or still compressed | Run `bash scripts/get_reference.sh` |
| STAR crashes or runs out of memory while indexing | Index too large for a small genome, or a half-built index | Keep `--genomeSAindexNbases 10`; delete `raw_data/star_index/` and rerun |
| STAR is very slow or the computer freezes | More threads than CPU cores | Lower `THREADS` in `ecoli_gene_quantification.sh` (check cores with `nproc`) |
| `ls: cannot access '*_1_val_1.fq.gz'` | Trimming not finished | Rerun Step 4 and check `raw_data/trimmed_reads/` |
| R: `Count files found: 0` | Wrong `training_dir`, or STAR not finished | Fix the path at the top of the R script; check `raw_data/star_align/` |
| Very few reads counted per gene | Wrong count column | Use `count_col <- 4` for this dataset |
| DESeq2: `stopifnot(...) are not all TRUE` | SRR IDs in `pdata.csv` don't match the count columns, or `pdata.csv` is still tab-separated | Compare `colnames(counts)` with `pdata$run_accession`; convert the file as in Step 1 |
| DESeq2: `model matrix is not full rank` | All samples ended up in one group | Check `table(pdata$group)` and the `sample_title` column |
| `could not find function "EnhancedVolcano"` | Package not installed | `BiocManager::install("EnhancedVolcano")` |

